freellmapi — https://github.com/tashfeenahmed/freellmapi
MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Tashfeen Ahmed

Reyaak's router is a native Kotlin reimplementation guided by this project's
design. Specifically informed by it:
  - the bandit routing score: signals normalized to [0,1] and combined as a
    convex combination, multiplied by always-on headroom and rate-limit
    guardrails, rather than a sum of hand-tuned bonuses;
  - Beta-posterior reliability with Thompson sampling, so exploration is
    proportional to uncertainty;
  - the saturating throughput curve and TTFB ramp forming a single speed axis,
    and the decision to charge timeouts against that axis;
  - tier-dominant intelligence scoring with square-root-compressed rank;
  - the upstream error taxonomy: which HTTP statuses are fail-over-able versus
    fatal, and why 403 and 413 belong in the former;
  - three-tier Retry-After resolution (header, then a walk of the error body for
    google.rpc.RetryInfo-shaped fields, then an anchored prose match), clamped;
  - the single-generic-adapter-plus-outliers structure for OpenAI-compatible
    providers.

