Hermes Agent — https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent
MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025 Nous Research

Reyaak's agent core is informed by this project's design. Specifically:
  - the separation of Memory (facts) from Skills (procedures);
  - the skill document model: frontmatter metadata plus a procedural body, with
    runtime state for version, lifecycle, pinning, and usage count;
  - skill authoring by prompting the live agent with authoring standards rather
    than building a separate distillation engine;
  - the curator's safety invariants, adopted verbatim as requirements: touch
    only agent-created skills, never auto-delete (archive, recoverably), let
    pinned items bypass all automatic transitions, and keep the expensive
    model-driven pass opt-in behind a cheap deterministic one;
  - inactivity-triggered maintenance in place of a scheduling daemon;
  - classifying tools by side-effect capability, with unknown and external
    tools treated as effect-capable by default.

